# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the test processes that keep the Graal isolate alive at exit
# (LSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=...): the exit, static initialization and isolate argument tests, the samples and the tools.
#
# The Graal native image is not instrumented; its allocations (the memory of the isolate runtime and of its threads)
# are alive when such a process exits: the library never tears the isolate down. The rule matches any frame of the SDK
# library, so it also hides a leak of the C++ library through the SDK (memory allocated by a callback and never freed,
# a handle never released). The tests of tests/main.cpp and the teardown scenarios of the exit test tear the isolate
# down at the end and run without this file where LeakSanitizer works (tests/CMakeLists.txt,
# DXFC_TEST_TEAR_DOWN_ISOLATE), so such leaks are reported there.
leak:libDxFeedGraalNativeSdk
